+``--audio-spdif-backoff=<yes|no>``
+    When a passthrough output fails while playing (on Apple platforms, the
+    AVPlayer and spatial audio outputs; each failure costs several seconds
+    before the PCM fallback), decode that codec to PCM on this audio route
+    instead of trying passthrough again on every file and output reload
+    (default: no, which retries on the next file or reload). It is kept per
+    codec and per player instance, and an entry lapses when the route
+    changes (on iOS and tvOS also when the route reports a device change,
+    the same device coming back included), after
+    ``--audio-spdif-backoff-expiry``, and once passthrough of any codec has
+    played on the same route for 10 seconds.
+
+``--audio-spdif-backoff-expiry=<seconds>``
+    How long a ``--audio-spdif-backoff`` entry lasts at most (default: 600).
+    0 keeps it until one of the other conditions clears it.
